From 12cee9a53da2a8003f311bee6da50bebefa935b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:31:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover libkern/os/metric.c

Reconstruct the production half of libkern/os/metric.c: the dropped
metric counter, the disabled check, the record builder, the log-queue
sender and the os_metric_coprocessor entry point.  Signature order,
locals and statement lines follow the KDK 27.0.1 DWARF; the bodies were
verified against the RELEASE and kasan vmapple kernels.

Also add the supporting declarations the file needs: os_metric_context_encode,
log_payload_init and get_os_log_subsystem_id, the shared os_log_mem, and the
metric_types.h record layout and size helper.

The DEVELOPMENT-only unit tests that follow the production code in the
reference file are not reproduced yet.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
